{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Final consolidation product as the run's total budget expires (action=research), referencing the eight retained direct-check executions rather than restating them. It records that six implementation responsibilities are confirmed in scope by executed clean-copy checks and correspondence reviews: the follower's cached last-log identity is not updated on the two appendEntries error returns, leaving the node rejecting otherwise valid AppendEntries for the truncated range (two independent scenarios); the leader answers inflight futures with ErrAbortedByRestore before the fallible snapshot creation, so a failed restore leaves a definite 'write effectively failed' signal on entries that remain logged; the monotonic-store snapshot install empties the log store without re-deriving the cached identity, so a follower whose cached index exceeds the installed snapshot index rejects the leader's post-install AppendEntries; FileSnapshotStore.List does not meet the SnapshotStore contract for an inversely ordered retained pair, inherited by both named consumers (the leader ships the lower-index snapshot, confirmed by its own check, and startup recovery adopts it, confirmed as its own recovery duty); and a bootstrap whose log write fails after the term write leaves the store looking already bootstrapped so the ordinary retry is rejected. It also states the remaining frontier: production reachability and any safety consequence of each confirmed defect; the two deferred surfaces (Restore error reporting, Apply future abandoned at shutdown); the FSM batch manager, tcp transport stream/pooling, TimeoutNow-without-term residual and part of startup reconstruction; and the open question whether the term-first comparator is the intended ordering. No map change is proposed because the map already records all six relationships, every previously deferred surface as